{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/statusbarguide"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The status bar is a row at the bottom of the terminal that shows keyboard shortcuts and contextual information. It updates every frame while it has active items."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The status bar is hidden automatically when there are no active user items and no visible system items."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit provides two status bar styles: "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarStyle\/compact","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (single-line, shortcuts only) and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarStyle\/bordered","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (bordered with title support)."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Architecture","text":"Architecture","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The status bar system has three parts:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarState","type":"reference"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Manages the item stack, style, and event handling","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarItem","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": A single shortcut entry (key + label + action)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBar","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]},{"type":"text","text":": The view that renders items into a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FrameBuffer"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Defining-Status-Bar-Items","text":"Defining Status Bar Items","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"statusBarItems","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier on your views to register shortcuts:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["VStack {","    Text(\"My App\")","}",".statusBarItems {","    StatusBarItem(shortcut: \"n\", label: \"new\") {","        \/\/ handle \"n\" key press","    }","    StatusBarItem(shortcut: \"d\", label: \"delete\") {","        \/\/ handle \"d\" key press","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Items are registered per frame during rendering. When a view is removed from the tree, its items automatically disappear from the status bar."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Shortcut-Display-Symbols","text":"Shortcut Display Symbols","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Shortcut"},{"type":"text","text":" to keep displayed shortcut symbols consistent:"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Constant","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Display"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Description"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Shortcut.quit"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Default quit display","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Shortcut.enter"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlin